ls on this head, passes with the posted fix.","refs":[{"id":"test/shell.d/menu-test.sh","kind":"file","line":875},{"id":"pocs/pr13012-back-from-search.js","kind":"file","line":1}],"title":"Back from a deeper search result (filtered drill-in)"},{"forClaim":9,"rationale":"Pins the stale-index fallback to root.","refs":[{"id":"shell/plugins/menu/Menu.qml","kind":"file","line":786}],"title":"Back after the parent menu is removed from the user file"},{"forClaim":10,"rationale":"Assert match() is non-null with a descriptive message, or extract each function on its own.","refs":[{"id":"test/shell.d/menu-test.sh","kind":"file","line":844}],"title":"Extraction guard in menu-test.sh navigation block"}],"summary":"**What the PR does.** Upstream #13012 (onurersel, head 7a7fb10c) changes Menu.qml setActiveMenu/goBack. A drill-in now pushes {menu, index, itemId} instead of a menu id. Back restores that index, then moves the cursor to the remembered row id if it is listed and selectable. The PR adds a vm test block to menu-test.sh. Mirror commit a38415fa is the upstream change. The other 13 commits are our proof work: SW-REQ-261001-B4CK, its witnesses in menu-pointer-lifecycle-test.sh, KI-MENU-BACK-FILTERED-INDEX with a PoC, REVIEW-261001-BFW5, the goBack annotation moved, and the trace re-review. This is an advisory audit, not an approval.\n\n**Is the fix verified?** No changed decision line is uncovered (diffCoverage measured). Tests: 53/53 passed, report current. B4CK has 2 observed passing tests, but its inherited boundary cell is unobserved. DE93, the parent behaviour, has no observed outcome: its only tests are the live compositor suite (known baseline gap). I ran the PR's test and the PoC: the PoC reproduces the KI at the head (Back lands on 'learn'); at the base Back lands on row 0.\n\n**Compatibility.** Readiness not_assessed. Next decision human_judgement (compat_changes_unapproved), reviewer under the approved policy @ 9f3abc10; 26 compat findings are unapproved and prevent readiness. All 24 mcdc_diff findings are witness-id renames: the same file, same scenarios, same rows. 21 come from the PR's own menu-test.sh block, 3 from a line our proof commit added. The 2 removed_behavior findings are the test regex signature update (intended, B4CK). The differential ran 213 inputs with 0 differences, but its harness does not drive navigation, so it says nothing about Back.\n\n**Questions for a human.** (1) Back after a deeper search result (KI, reproduced). (2) A removed parent menu applies a stale index to root. (3) The PR's extraction regex throws when a comment sits above goBack.\n\n**Traceability.** setActiveMenu is traced to DE93 and B4CK. 35 requirements are code_changed only through file-level traces. 11 spec-gap candidates are all bindings inside our PoC (a KI reproducer, not product code). Change effects were not analyzed.\n\n**Not caused by this PR.** 10 test_outcome_unobserved disclosures come from the live Hyprland/Quickshell suites, which no audit suite runs. No gate fails."}
